1
00:00:14,615 --> 00:00:19,953
HELLO, TWENTY - WONHEE

2
00:00:20,354 --> 00:00:23,323
ONE FINE DAY WITH DAZZLING SUNLIGHT

3
00:00:24,024 --> 00:00:27,027
AND LUSH GREEN LEAVES

4
00:00:27,394 --> 00:00:29,363
Hello, today,

5
00:00:29,429 --> 00:00:33,400
I can't wait to see
what new experience is in store for me.

6
00:00:33,567 --> 00:00:36,270
What's waiting for me
in this special place?

7
00:00:36,336 --> 00:00:38,472
Can you guess where we are?

8
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:39,540
A Buddhist temple.

9
00:00:40,407 --> 00:00:42,509
A TEMPLE?

10
00:00:42,809 --> 00:00:44,378
Have you ever visited one?

11
00:00:44,444 --> 00:00:46,847
I've always wanted to
whenever I had a lot on my mind,

12
00:00:46,914 --> 00:00:48,615
so I had a few pinned on the map.

13
00:00:48,682 --> 00:00:52,319
I've never actually visited one,
so I'm happy to be here.

14
00:00:52,486 --> 00:00:54,021
I'll share today's theme.

15
00:00:54,087 --> 00:00:59,293
People in their 20s are starting
to realize the importance of self-care.

16
00:00:59,359 --> 00:01:01,328
Of course, that's very important.

17
00:01:01,395 --> 00:01:04,131
YOU LEARN TO CARE FOR YOURSELF AT 20

18
00:01:04,398 --> 00:01:07,301
YOUNG ADULTS IN THEIR 20S
NEED TIME TO FOCUS ON THEMSELVES

19
00:01:07,568 --> 00:01:09,703
SIXTH ITEM ON WONHEE'S BUCKET LIST

20
00:01:09,870 --> 00:01:12,139
TEMPLE STAY

21
00:01:12,205 --> 00:01:15,409
Today is your chance to look inward

22
00:01:15,475 --> 00:01:18,845
and care for both your mind and body.

23
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:21,214
TEMPLE STAY, FOCUSING ON MINDFULNESS

24
00:01:21,281 --> 00:01:22,549
Why don't you call today's guest?

25
00:01:23,283 --> 00:01:25,385
Girlie!

26
00:01:26,119 --> 00:01:27,187
Wonhee!

27
00:01:27,254 --> 00:01:28,889
- Hello.
- Hello.

28
00:01:28,956 --> 00:01:31,258
It's nice to meet you.
You look so adorable.

29
00:01:31,325 --> 00:01:32,893
EPISODE 6 GIRLIE
MIYEON OF I-DLE

30
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:34,094
Gosh, thank you.

31
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:37,397
SLIGHTLY AWKWARD

32
00:01:37,464 --> 00:01:39,967
- We've never had a proper chat before.
- Right?

33
00:01:40,033 --> 00:01:42,869
We've only said hello
when we were on the same music show.

34
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:44,504
- Right.
- "Hello."

35
00:01:44,571 --> 00:01:45,739
Our interactions

36
00:01:45,806 --> 00:01:48,008
- only lasted a fraction of a second.
- Honestly,

37
00:01:48,075 --> 00:01:50,611
I see you on my social media all the time.

38
00:01:50,677 --> 00:01:54,281
I already feel like we're friends.

39
00:01:54,348 --> 00:01:56,917
I didn't know you turned 20 this year.

40
00:01:56,984 --> 00:01:59,119
- Really?
- I thought you'd still be a teenager.

41
00:01:59,186 --> 00:02:00,988
- I'm legal this year.
- Seriously?

42
00:02:01,054 --> 00:02:02,789
No, don't be.

43
00:02:02,856 --> 00:02:03,790
ASTOUNDED

44
00:02:03,857 --> 00:02:05,258
I can't believe it.

45
00:02:05,325 --> 00:02:07,327
We'd have to cancel this show, then.

46
00:02:07,394 --> 00:02:09,162
STAY 20 FOREVER, WONHEE

47
00:02:10,163 --> 00:02:12,165
- Hello.
- Hello.

48
00:02:12,232 --> 00:02:13,066
HERE'S THEIR GUIDE

49
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,901
- It's nice to meet you.
- Likewise.

50
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:18,271
I guide participants in the temple stay
here at Seokbulsa Temple.

51
00:02:18,338 --> 00:02:19,906
I'm Bhikshuni Yeomok.

52
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:21,375
- Bhikshuni Yeomok.
- That's right.

53
00:02:21,441 --> 00:02:24,111
My Dharma name means "like trees."

54
00:02:24,177 --> 00:02:26,647
During your temple stay program,

55
00:02:26,713 --> 00:02:28,882
I'll be your tree to rest under.

56
00:02:28,949 --> 00:02:30,684
Thank you.

57
00:02:30,751 --> 00:02:32,686
We'll get started shortly.

58
00:02:32,753 --> 00:02:34,955
Let's get changed
into temple stay uniforms.

59
00:02:35,022 --> 00:02:36,023
- Yes.
- Of course.

60
00:02:36,089 --> 00:02:39,793
Our cute outfits will barely get
any screen time.

61
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:41,028
Goodbye now.

62
00:02:41,928 --> 00:02:43,063
One, two, three.

63
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:44,064
A LITTLE KEEPSAKE

64
00:02:44,431 --> 00:02:45,899
BEFORE LEAVING THE SECULAR WORLD

65
00:02:45,966 --> 00:02:47,601
<i>- Let's get changed.</i>
<i>- Okay.</i>

66
00:02:47,668 --> 00:02:49,336
OFF THEY GO TO GET CHANGED

67
00:02:49,403 --> 00:02:51,938
Wonhee and Miyeon,
you look great in the uniform.

68
00:02:52,005 --> 00:02:53,840
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

69
00:02:54,074 --> 00:02:56,343
For our temple stay program,

70
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:59,613
we'll first take a stroll
to get to know more about the temple.

71
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:04,251
<i>- Next, we'll have a tea break.</i>
<i>- Sounds good.</i>

72
00:03:04,317 --> 00:03:06,053
<i>We'll make prayer beads through 108 bows</i>

73
00:03:06,119 --> 00:03:07,421
<i>and try meditation as well.</i>

74
00:03:07,487 --> 00:03:08,822
And lastly,

75
00:03:08,889 --> 00:03:11,324
hoping your wishes will come true,

76
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:14,428
<i>- we'll light a candle for each of you.</i>
<i>- A candle? I see.</i>

77
00:03:14,494 --> 00:03:17,431
How does that plan sound to you?

78
00:03:17,497 --> 00:03:18,331
- Amazing.
- Lovely.

79
00:03:18,398 --> 00:03:19,700
- Are you looking forward to it?
- Yes.

80
00:03:19,766 --> 00:03:21,068
TOUR OF THE TEMPLE
<i>Shall we, then?</i>

81
00:03:21,134 --> 00:03:22,536
<i>- Okay.</i>
<i>- Sure!</i>

82
00:03:23,370 --> 00:03:25,205
We're in the presence of Buddha.

83
00:03:25,572 --> 00:03:28,942
BUDDHA STATUE STANDING GUARD
<i>Press your palms together like this.</i>

84
00:03:29,009 --> 00:03:32,546
This gesture means,
"I respect you with all my heart."

85
00:03:32,713 --> 00:03:34,715
We'll greet Buddha.

86
00:03:34,781 --> 00:03:37,684
NEW FOLLOWERS GREET BUDDHA
FOR THE FIRST TIME

87
00:03:37,751 --> 00:03:40,654
This statue here is Maitreya Buddha.

88
00:03:40,721 --> 00:03:41,955
- Maitreya Buddha.
- That's right.

89
00:03:42,022 --> 00:03:45,859
Maitreya Buddha speaks to us
through his hand gestures.

90
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:48,762
<i>Can you guess what each gesture means?</i>

91
00:03:48,829 --> 00:03:51,031
- What does this mean?
- Right, you hold it up like this.

92
00:03:51,098 --> 00:03:54,234
His left hand is pointing downward
with his palm showing.

93
00:03:54,301 --> 00:03:59,706
That means, "Tell me what you desire.
I will make your wishes come true."

94
00:03:59,773 --> 00:04:04,177
He's inviting us to share our worries
and wishes with him

95
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:08,148
- so that he can help us.
- He's offering to help?

96
00:04:08,215 --> 00:04:09,282
Now the right hand.

97
00:04:09,349 --> 00:04:12,252
It means that
since he will look out for us,

98
00:04:12,319 --> 00:04:16,823
we can live confidently and peacefully,
free from concerns.

99
00:04:18,024 --> 00:04:20,827
- In other words, "Don't be afraid."
- Because he'll be there for us?

100
00:04:21,495 --> 00:04:23,263
- That's so nice.
- That's his message.

101
00:04:23,330 --> 00:04:24,931
During the program,

102
00:04:24,998 --> 00:04:27,367
feel free to share your burdens
before Buddha.

103
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:28,568
Hopefully, when you leave,

104
00:04:28,635 --> 00:04:31,538
you'll be confident, peaceful,
and free of worries.

105
00:04:31,605 --> 00:04:33,607
- Let's make that happen.
- Yes, ma'am.

106
00:04:33,974 --> 00:04:34,841
- Okay.
- Sounds great.

107
00:04:34,908 --> 00:04:36,910
- Shall we go to the Daeungjeon Hall?
- Yes.

108
00:04:37,544 --> 00:04:39,246
<i>So that's what the gestures meant.</i>

109
00:04:39,312 --> 00:04:40,547
OFF TO THE NEXT SITE

110
00:04:40,781 --> 00:04:43,850
- The panel reads "Daeungjeon Hall."
- Yes.

111
00:04:43,917 --> 00:04:46,987
<i>As the name suggests,</i>
<i>this hall is dedicated to the Great Hero.</i>

112
00:04:47,053 --> 00:04:48,355
<i>Let's go inside.</i>

113
00:04:48,421 --> 00:04:50,390
When you visit a shrine
in a Buddhist temple,

114
00:04:50,457 --> 00:04:52,559
you greet Buddha right upon entry.

115
00:04:52,726 --> 00:04:54,528
Turn toward the statue,
press your palms together,

116
00:04:55,328 --> 00:04:56,630
and take a half bow.

117
00:04:57,364 --> 00:04:58,532
After that,

118
00:04:58,598 --> 00:05:01,835
we'll take a full bow
known as the five-point prostration.

119
00:05:01,902 --> 00:05:05,372
Our bodies' 5 points,
including 2 knees, 2 elbows,

120
00:05:05,438 --> 00:05:07,307
and the forehead, should touch the floor.

121
00:05:07,374 --> 00:05:10,210
We pay our respects
in the humblest posture.

122
00:05:11,144 --> 00:05:11,978
- For the bow?
- Yes.

123
00:05:12,045 --> 00:05:14,147
- We all have sharp, thorny impulses.
- Of course.

124
00:05:14,214 --> 00:05:17,083
Greed and anger fall into that category.

125
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:19,886
As we kneel and bow,
we leave them on the floor.

126
00:05:19,953 --> 00:05:21,721
- "Sharp, thorny impulses."
- Exactly.

127
00:05:21,788 --> 00:05:22,889
Once you let them go,

128
00:05:22,956 --> 00:05:27,394
<i>it'll be like the clouds parting</i>
<i>to reveal the sun.</i>

129
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:29,996
You'll find clarity in your minds as well.

130
00:05:30,063 --> 00:05:32,365
With that, we'll rise.

131
00:05:32,699 --> 00:05:34,034
When you visit a Buddhist temple,

132
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:37,037
the common etiquette is
to bow three times.

133
00:05:37,103 --> 00:05:38,071
Shall we, then?

134
00:05:38,138 --> 00:05:40,373
- Let's bow to Buddha three times.
- Sure.

135
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:42,576
All right. Press your palms together

136
00:05:42,642 --> 00:05:45,011
and take a half bow.

137
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:46,913
Kneel.

138
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:47,948
COPY AND PASTE

139
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:49,950
Next, place your hands on the floor.

140
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,818
Rest your elbows on the floor.

141
00:05:51,885 --> 00:05:53,220
Let your forehead meet the floor.

142
00:05:53,286 --> 00:05:55,622
Turn your hands over
and raise them to your ears.

143
00:05:55,689 --> 00:05:56,690
Now lower them.

144
00:05:56,990 --> 00:05:58,525
LIKE THIS?
There you go.

145
00:05:58,592 --> 00:06:00,827
Press your palms together again.

146
00:06:00,894 --> 00:06:01,728
HALF A BEAT LATE

147
00:06:01,795 --> 00:06:03,697
Push through your feet and stand up.

148
00:06:03,763 --> 00:06:04,731
There we go.

149
00:06:05,232 --> 00:06:06,066
Well done.

150
00:06:06,132 --> 00:06:08,501
Let's take our second bow.
Repeat the process.

151
00:06:11,238 --> 00:06:14,341
RARE SIGHT OF WONHEE BEING SERIOUS

152
00:06:14,407 --> 00:06:17,444
Lastly, because the third bow
is our last one,

153
00:06:17,510 --> 00:06:19,613
we'll lift our forehead a bit

154
00:06:19,679 --> 00:06:21,548
and place our hands underneath.

155
00:06:21,615 --> 00:06:23,917
- Do you have a wish?
- Yes.

156
00:06:23,984 --> 00:06:26,720
Share it with Buddha in your mind.

157
00:06:26,786 --> 00:06:27,821
PLEASE LET THEM COME TRUE

158
00:06:27,988 --> 00:06:29,356
Then we can stand back up.

159
00:06:31,825 --> 00:06:33,693
Now the finish.

160
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,061
SUCCESSFUL FIRST MEETING

161
00:06:35,128 --> 00:06:37,230
After the three bows,

162
00:06:37,297 --> 00:06:40,867
simply rest in Buddha's presence.

163
00:06:40,934 --> 00:06:41,835
All right.

164
00:06:41,902 --> 00:06:43,570
Now that we have greeted Buddha,

165
00:06:43,637 --> 00:06:47,240
- let's go have tea together.
- Okay.

166
00:06:50,176 --> 00:06:53,580
Wow, I'm surprised to see
all these different buildings.

167
00:06:53,647 --> 00:06:55,415
- Please come on in.
- Okay.

168
00:06:56,216 --> 00:06:57,417
Here we are.

169
00:06:58,485 --> 00:06:59,486
<i>This way.</i>

170
00:06:59,552 --> 00:07:01,554
COZY AND QUIET

171
00:07:01,821 --> 00:07:06,860
TEATIME WITH BHIKSHUNI YEOMOK

172
00:07:07,127 --> 00:07:09,229
- Make yourselves at home.
- Okay.

173
00:07:10,297 --> 00:07:12,032
SUPER RESPECTFUL POSE

174
00:07:12,299 --> 00:07:13,400
STARES

175
00:07:13,466 --> 00:07:14,301
Are you comfortable?

176
00:07:14,367 --> 00:07:16,136
- You don't have to kneel.
- Really?

177
00:07:16,202 --> 00:07:17,370
- Of course.
- How should I sit?

178
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:19,339
- You can just...
- I wanted to be respectful.

179
00:07:19,406 --> 00:07:21,675
Fold the back of the cushion like I did.

180
00:07:22,375 --> 00:07:23,977
- It's so comfy.
- Really?

181
00:07:24,044 --> 00:07:25,545
- Much better?
- Yes.

182
00:07:25,612 --> 00:07:26,746
There we go.

183
00:07:26,813 --> 00:07:28,481
SET FREE

184
00:07:28,682 --> 00:07:30,884
We'll be having five-flavored berry tea.

185
00:07:30,951 --> 00:07:33,086
As its name suggests,
it has all five flavors.

186
00:07:33,153 --> 00:07:34,354
Can you guess them all?

187
00:07:34,421 --> 00:07:37,290
Salty, sweet, sour...

188
00:07:37,357 --> 00:07:38,825
I swear I know them all.

189
00:07:38,892 --> 00:07:40,894
I love five-flavored berries.

190
00:07:40,961 --> 00:07:43,029
- Shall we try it first, then?
- Okay.

191
00:07:44,431 --> 00:07:45,265
Here you go.

192
00:07:45,332 --> 00:07:46,766
Such a pretty color.

193
00:07:46,833 --> 00:07:49,636
Hold your hand like this
and rest your teacup on it.

194
00:07:50,637 --> 00:07:51,972
Think of today's teatime

195
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:56,543
as your gift for yourself,
the most precious person in the world.

196
00:07:56,609 --> 00:07:58,945
- A gift for myself.
- Yes, that's it.

197
00:07:59,012 --> 00:08:00,580
Hold up your cup,

198
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:01,881
gaze at it,

199
00:08:02,649 --> 00:08:04,684
and appreciate its aroma.

200
00:08:04,751 --> 00:08:05,719
TEA ETIQUETTE

201
00:08:05,785 --> 00:08:07,287
Taste it.

202
00:08:07,354 --> 00:08:09,589
TAKE A SIP

203
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:10,991
MHM

204
00:08:11,057 --> 00:08:12,826
It tastes better this way.

205
00:08:12,892 --> 00:08:13,727
All right.

206
00:08:14,627 --> 00:08:17,664
- Have you figured it out?
- Sour, sweet,

207
00:08:17,731 --> 00:08:19,566
- salty, bitter...
- That's right.

208
00:08:19,632 --> 00:08:20,633
What comes next?

209
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:22,202
I can't recall the last one.

210
00:08:22,268 --> 00:08:23,169
SO ELUSIVE

211
00:08:23,236 --> 00:08:25,071
LAST ANSWER: SPICY

212
00:08:25,138 --> 00:08:28,708
Now that we've had a sip,
let's have a chat.

213
00:08:28,775 --> 00:08:31,344
Feel free to ask me anything.

214
00:08:31,411 --> 00:08:32,579
WONHEE FIRST
Ma'am.

215
00:08:32,645 --> 00:08:35,782
How do you handle stress?

216
00:08:35,982 --> 00:08:38,752
I tend to avoid stressful situations.

217
00:08:38,818 --> 00:08:40,587
What if they're unavoidable?

218
00:08:40,653 --> 00:08:42,122
They're unavoidable?

219
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:43,456
All right, then.

220
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:45,558
- I'll have to bear it.
- The stress?

221
00:08:45,625 --> 00:08:47,727
No, the situation itself.

222
00:08:47,794 --> 00:08:50,163
- I'll have to ride it out.
- Ride it out?

223
00:08:50,230 --> 00:08:55,335
Or you can try shifting your focus
away from the stressful situation.

224
00:08:55,402 --> 00:08:57,504
You can leave it behind,
just like you did today.

225
00:08:57,570 --> 00:08:58,838
AS THEY FOUND REFUGE IN THE TEMPLE

226
00:08:58,905 --> 00:09:01,074
Even as your emotions rage like a storm,

227
00:09:01,141 --> 00:09:04,244
take time to understand
what your heart truly wants.

228
00:09:04,944 --> 00:09:08,181
Ask yourself
how you would like to lead your life.

229
00:09:08,248 --> 00:09:11,451
I think moments like that
call for self-reflection.

230
00:09:11,518 --> 00:09:13,286
GAIN A BETTER UNDERSTANDING OF YOURSELF

231
00:09:13,686 --> 00:09:15,088
Take a short nap,

232
00:09:15,155 --> 00:09:17,090
- take a shower,
- That's a good idea.

233
00:09:17,157 --> 00:09:18,158
or clean your room.

234
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:19,759
Oh, cleaning.

235
00:09:19,826 --> 00:09:22,629
I clean my room daily these days.

236
00:09:22,695 --> 00:09:26,099
- That's a great habit.
- It's therapeutic.

237
00:09:26,166 --> 00:09:29,102
I decorate and clean my room.

238
00:09:29,169 --> 00:09:31,004
- It's my little therapy.
- Really?

239
00:09:31,071 --> 00:09:32,806
Cleaning gives me so much stress.

240
00:09:33,473 --> 00:09:34,808
Can I visit to clean sometime?

241
00:09:34,874 --> 00:09:36,176
- Hit me up anytime.
- Oh, no.

242
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:37,243
I'D LOVE TO DO THAT

243
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:39,079
Don't you have any questions, Miyeon?

244
00:09:39,145 --> 00:09:41,114
I lack self-control.

245
00:09:41,181 --> 00:09:44,150
The world is full of amazing...

246
00:09:44,884 --> 00:09:46,619
LET ME DRINK THIS TEA FIRST

247
00:09:46,686 --> 00:09:48,388
...snacks.

248
00:09:48,455 --> 00:09:52,292
<i>Whenever I see them,</i>
<i>I can't control myself.</i>

249
00:09:52,358 --> 00:09:55,562
How do I build self-restraint?

250
00:09:55,628 --> 00:09:58,164
This doesn't apply to appetite alone.

251
00:09:58,231 --> 00:10:02,268
Suppressing your urges
is stressful in general.

252
00:10:02,335 --> 00:10:03,770
- Right?
- Exactly.

253
00:10:03,837 --> 00:10:06,072
As followers of Buddha,
we practice patience.

254
00:10:06,139 --> 00:10:08,908
PATIENCE: SPIRITUAL VIRTUE OF ENDURING
AND BEARING HARDSHIP

255
00:10:08,975 --> 00:10:10,977
But in your case,

256
00:10:11,044 --> 00:10:13,213
you're repressing an urge
that is already there.

257
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:15,482
You're forcing yourself to behave.

258
00:10:15,548 --> 00:10:19,119
"Don't get mad.
Don't be depressed. Don't be sad."

259
00:10:19,185 --> 00:10:21,221
Do you tend to hold back your anger?

260
00:10:21,287 --> 00:10:22,589
- I don't.
- I do.

261
00:10:23,056 --> 00:10:25,258
As a celebrity,
you have to hold it in, right?

262
00:10:25,325 --> 00:10:26,426
I tend to let it go.

263
00:10:26,493 --> 00:10:27,460
Do you?

264
00:10:27,527 --> 00:10:28,761
You're cool that way.

265
00:10:28,828 --> 00:10:30,797
- She's pretty cool.
- I see.

266
00:10:30,864 --> 00:10:33,566
Those who hold back
may think it'd be satisfying.

267
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:34,934
Isn't it?

268
00:10:35,001 --> 00:10:36,603
It leaves you with regrets.

269
00:10:36,669 --> 00:10:37,504
After an outburst,

270
00:10:37,570 --> 00:10:39,272
- you're left with regret.
- That's true.

271
00:10:39,339 --> 00:10:41,007
But when you hold it in,
you end up with stress.

272
00:10:41,074 --> 00:10:42,542
What a headache, right?

273
00:10:42,609 --> 00:10:43,877
Could we combine our personalities?

274
00:10:43,943 --> 00:10:45,912
UNIFICATION ATTEMPT

275
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:49,816
You know, patience isn't
just about denying your urges.

276
00:10:49,883 --> 00:10:51,818
It's about giving yourself time.

277
00:10:52,619 --> 00:10:56,322
Your emotions may surge like a tidal wave,
but don't let them take over.

278
00:10:56,389 --> 00:11:00,827
Instead, take a moment
to think about what you truly want.

279
00:11:00,894 --> 00:11:02,829
Rather than suppressing your urges,

280
00:11:02,896 --> 00:11:06,366
think of it as a chance
to take better care of yourself.

281
00:11:06,432 --> 00:11:07,967
That way, you avoid the stress.

282
00:11:08,468 --> 00:11:11,538
Would I have to think first
when I get angry?

283
00:11:11,604 --> 00:11:13,173
No, you need to stop thinking.

284
00:11:13,239 --> 00:11:14,374
- Stop it?
- Yes.

285
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:16,876
Don't get caught up in your thoughts.

286
00:11:16,943 --> 00:11:17,777
Take a pause.

287
00:11:17,844 --> 00:11:22,749
Then you'll have the clarity to see
what your heart truly wants.

288
00:11:22,815 --> 00:11:27,754
You can make a decision you won't regret.

289
00:11:27,820 --> 00:11:30,623
What should I do
when I'm worried about the future?

290
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:32,926
So many participants
share the same concern.

291
00:11:32,992 --> 00:11:35,361
"The world changes so fast.

292
00:11:35,428 --> 00:11:38,598
I'm afraid I can't keep up
with the speed."

293
00:11:38,665 --> 00:11:40,533
It makes them anxious.

294
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,203
If you let your worries take over,
they become a habit.

295
00:11:43,736 --> 00:11:45,705
- Don't let it become a habit.
- Exactly.

296
00:11:46,306 --> 00:11:47,207
WHAT'S UP WITH HER?

297
00:11:47,273 --> 00:11:48,141
Don't let it become--

298
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:50,176
She's so serious.

299
00:11:50,243 --> 00:11:52,745
Just what is eating you up so much?

300
00:11:52,812 --> 00:11:53,947
CAN'T EVEN IMAGINE

301
00:11:54,013 --> 00:11:55,882
Maybe she's just very curious.

302
00:11:55,949 --> 00:11:58,251
THIS YOUNG FOLLOWER
IS CURIOUS ABOUT EVERYTHING

303
00:11:58,685 --> 00:12:00,186
NOW I KNOW
Don't let it become a habit.

304
00:12:00,253 --> 00:12:03,690
Honestly, it's so nice

305
00:12:03,756 --> 00:12:06,025
that your advice is clear and practical.

306
00:12:06,092 --> 00:12:08,194
Let's practice meditation later.

307
00:12:08,261 --> 00:12:11,998
We'll reflect on our wishes
while making prayer beads

308
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:13,900
- through 108 bows.
- Okay.

309
00:12:13,967 --> 00:12:15,868
- Why don't we finish the tea?
- Okay.

310
00:12:16,102 --> 00:12:17,570
NOT WASTING A DROP

311
00:12:17,637 --> 00:12:19,105
- Shall we?
- Yes.

312
00:12:19,672 --> 00:12:21,074
PRAYER BEADS THROUGH 108 BOWS

313
00:12:21,140 --> 00:12:23,643
<i>We'll now make prayer beads</i>
<i>through 108 bows.</i>

314
00:12:23,710 --> 00:12:25,478
Have you ever seen prayer beads?

315
00:12:25,545 --> 00:12:27,113
- Yes.
- Yes, as a bracelet.

316
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:29,682
The prayer beads we're going to make

317
00:12:29,749 --> 00:12:33,152
will help us count
as we practice 108 bows.

318
00:12:33,219 --> 00:12:36,522
The prayer beads literally mean
"beads of the mind."

319
00:12:36,689 --> 00:12:41,261
They're a reminder to keep Buddha
in our hearts and minds.

320
00:12:41,327 --> 00:12:43,730
While that is their main purpose,

321
00:12:43,796 --> 00:12:47,100
they're also helpful
when your mind is on a roller coaster.

322
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:50,670
In such times,
they can help you find composure.

323
00:12:50,737 --> 00:12:54,507
Counting the beads
will help calm your mind.

324
00:12:54,574 --> 00:12:58,244
First, why don't you open
the plastic bag with the beads?

325
00:12:58,645 --> 00:13:00,713
Now pour them into the bowl.

326
00:13:01,314 --> 00:13:02,482
BEADS TO HELP EMPTY YOUR MIND

327
00:13:02,548 --> 00:13:03,816
All right. Good.

328
00:13:04,150 --> 00:13:05,051
Do you see a string?

329
00:13:05,118 --> 00:13:06,753
Form a knot on one end.

330
00:13:06,819 --> 00:13:08,254
Don't make it too tight, though.

331
00:13:08,321 --> 00:13:11,858
We're only tying up one end
so that the beads don't fall out.

332
00:13:11,924 --> 00:13:13,826
Don't tighten it. Keep it loose.

333
00:13:14,394 --> 00:13:15,662
Good. Next.

334
00:13:15,728 --> 00:13:21,401
I'll recite <i>108 Bows to Happiness</i>
as you practice bowing.

335
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:24,237
After reading each item on the list,

336
00:13:24,304 --> 00:13:26,472
I'll strike the bamboo clapper.
You can bow then.

337
00:13:26,706 --> 00:13:30,476
As you come back up,
thread one bead onto the string.

338
00:13:30,543 --> 00:13:32,145
Just one bead.

339
00:13:32,445 --> 00:13:34,314
Then sit like this
with your palms together.

340
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:36,716
You'll thread 1 bead after 1 bow.

341
00:13:36,783 --> 00:13:37,684
UNDERSTOOD

342
00:13:37,750 --> 00:13:39,018
- That's it.
- I get it.

343
00:13:39,385 --> 00:13:40,286
108-BOW SESSION BEGINS

344
00:13:40,353 --> 00:13:41,654
Press your palms together.

345
00:13:42,021 --> 00:13:43,089
Half bow.

346
00:13:43,623 --> 00:13:44,457
SLIDES DOWN

347
00:13:44,524 --> 00:13:45,391
- Half bow.
- Half bow?

348
00:13:45,458 --> 00:13:46,292
Again.

349
00:13:46,359 --> 00:13:48,261
- Half bow.
- Do a half bow before a full one.

350
00:13:48,795 --> 00:13:50,029
2ND ATTEMPT

351
00:13:50,396 --> 00:13:52,765
A PROPER HALF BOW THIS TIME

352
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:56,569
"With utmost appreciation
and respect toward all living beings,

353
00:13:56,636 --> 00:13:59,439
we now take a bow."

354
00:13:59,872 --> 00:14:00,707
SNAP

355
00:14:01,607 --> 00:14:02,809
BOWS AT THE SNAP

356
00:14:02,875 --> 00:14:05,211
That's right.
Place your palms on the floor.

357
00:14:05,278 --> 00:14:07,980
Raise your torso and thread one bead.

358
00:14:09,082 --> 00:14:13,453
ONE LESS CONCERN FOR EVERY BEAD

359
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:14,654
SNAP

360
00:14:15,054 --> 00:14:16,255
On your feet now.

361
00:14:16,322 --> 00:14:17,423
ENDLESS CYCLE OF BOWS BEGINS

362
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:20,326
"As we humble ourselves
to control our ill tempers,

363
00:14:20,393 --> 00:14:23,096
we now take a bow."

364
00:14:23,162 --> 00:14:23,996
SNAP

365
00:14:25,064 --> 00:14:27,900
<i>The world is full of amazing snacks.</i>

366
00:14:27,967 --> 00:14:29,936
REPENTING OBSESSION WITH FOOD
<i>I can't control myself.</i>

367
00:14:30,002 --> 00:14:32,505
<i>What should I do</i>
<i>when I'm worried about the future?</i>

368
00:14:32,572 --> 00:14:34,440
LETTING GO OF HER FEARS ABOUT THE FUTURE

369
00:14:38,578 --> 00:14:39,779
FUMBLES

370
00:14:39,846 --> 00:14:41,547
THREADS A BEAD IN A FLASH

371
00:14:41,781 --> 00:14:43,783
THEY'RE NOT AT THE SAME SKILL LEVEL

372
00:14:44,650 --> 00:14:48,187
THE EXPERIENCE TURNS
INTO A JOURNEY OF TROUBLES

373
00:14:51,791 --> 00:14:53,659
WHEN WONHEE COMPLETES HER THREADING

374
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:55,728
MIYEON JUST GETS READY

375
00:14:56,162 --> 00:14:56,996
SNAP

376
00:14:58,030 --> 00:14:59,065
RUSHING

377
00:14:59,132 --> 00:15:01,501
"May we not misunderstand others..."

378
00:15:02,301 --> 00:15:04,604
SCRAMBLING

379
00:15:06,339 --> 00:15:08,341
JUST A SECOND... THAT WAS TOO FAST

380
00:15:08,541 --> 00:15:09,942
MIYEON, SPEED UP

381
00:15:12,412 --> 00:15:13,446
THERE GOES THE BEAD

382
00:15:13,513 --> 00:15:14,914
RUSHING

383
00:15:15,281 --> 00:15:17,417
A TIMING GAME BEGINS

384
00:15:21,788 --> 00:15:24,690
BEATS OF 108-BOW EXPERIENCE
WILL CONFUSE YOU

385
00:15:25,024 --> 00:15:26,859
GATHERS HERSELF TO FOCUS

386
00:15:27,427 --> 00:15:28,261
SNAP

387
00:15:29,295 --> 00:15:30,930
I'M GIVING UP
What on earth?

388
00:15:31,297 --> 00:15:32,765
How are you managing it?

389
00:15:32,832 --> 00:15:35,067
- Take your time and rise.
- Just do it.

390
00:15:35,368 --> 00:15:37,069
I CAN'T, THOUGH

391
00:15:37,503 --> 00:15:40,940
AS FOR WONHEE

392
00:15:41,374 --> 00:15:43,276
SHE NAILS IT EVERY TIME

393
00:15:43,543 --> 00:15:45,111
A SKILLED PRAYER BEADS MAKER

394
00:15:45,378 --> 00:15:47,713
AM I THREADING THE BEADS

395
00:15:48,047 --> 00:15:50,483
OR ARE THE BEADS SOMEHOW THREADING ME?

396
00:15:50,550 --> 00:15:52,251
ONE WITH THE BEADS

397
00:15:52,585 --> 00:15:53,953
PERFECT HARMONY

398
00:15:58,591 --> 00:16:00,993
SOMEWHERE BETWEEN TRAINING AND SUFFERING

399
00:16:01,227 --> 00:16:03,396
THEY LET GO OF THEIR WORRIES AND DESIRES

400
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:05,498
JUST WHEN THE DOPAMINE RUSH
IS ABOUT TO HIT THEM...

401
00:16:05,798 --> 00:16:07,800
This is our last bow.

402
00:16:07,867 --> 00:16:09,035
FINALLY, THE LAST ONE

403
00:16:12,205 --> 00:16:15,775
"May our 108 wishes come true."

404
00:16:16,008 --> 00:16:17,677
Thread your last bead.

405
00:16:19,011 --> 00:16:21,848
ONE LAST BEAD
TO TAKE THEIR LAST CONCERN AWAY

406
00:16:21,914 --> 00:16:23,950
There. Make sure to tighten the knot.

407
00:16:24,016 --> 00:16:25,051
Tie them together.

408
00:16:25,318 --> 00:16:27,220
WITH A KNOT SECURELY TIED

409
00:16:27,286 --> 00:16:28,821
Fasten the knot.

410
00:16:29,689 --> 00:16:32,058
<i>You have your prayer beads now.</i>

411
00:16:32,124 --> 00:16:37,497
Your 108 worries have become prayer beads
filled with new wishes.

412
00:16:38,164 --> 00:16:39,665
PRAYER BEADS OBTAINED

413
00:16:39,732 --> 00:16:40,967
Thank you.

414
00:16:41,467 --> 00:16:45,638
<i>Let's wrap up with a meditation</i>
<i>to calm our minds.</i>

415
00:16:46,672 --> 00:16:47,673
- What was that?
- A bug.

416
00:16:48,841 --> 00:16:50,877
Oh, no. Killing is forbidden, right?

417
00:16:52,311 --> 00:16:53,779
WHAT DO I DO?

418
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:55,081
Go on. Set it free.

419
00:16:55,147 --> 00:16:58,117
It's still alive.

420
00:16:58,851 --> 00:17:00,853
Bye.

421
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:02,755
- It might've survived.
- I'm sure it did.

422
00:17:02,822 --> 00:17:04,790
It just got knocked out.

423
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:07,994
MEDITATION TIME
Sit up straight.

424
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:10,463
Straighten your back and sit up properly.

425
00:17:10,663 --> 00:17:13,199
Hold up your right hand
as we did earlier during the teatime.

426
00:17:13,533 --> 00:17:15,301
Place your left hand on top of it.

427
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:18,137
Make a circle with your thumbs.

428
00:17:18,404 --> 00:17:19,405
Open your chest.

429
00:17:19,472 --> 00:17:20,873
CRACK

430
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:22,074
Did I hear something?

431
00:17:22,141 --> 00:17:23,743
Not at all.

432
00:17:23,809 --> 00:17:24,810
Did you hear anything?

433
00:17:25,211 --> 00:17:26,746
THEY HAVE EACH OTHER'S BACKS
No.

434
00:17:26,979 --> 00:17:28,681
Close your eyes.

435
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:30,550
There you go.

436
00:17:30,616 --> 00:17:33,686
Next, take a deep breath in.

437
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,256
Exhale.

438
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:39,926
Imagine your body
filling up like a balloon.

439
00:17:40,192 --> 00:17:42,762
Focus on controlling our breath.

440
00:17:49,535 --> 00:17:50,503
EYES WIDE OPEN

441
00:17:52,171 --> 00:17:54,740
LOST FOCUS

442
00:17:56,008 --> 00:17:58,744
LOCKING IN AGAIN

443
00:18:03,616 --> 00:18:07,653
FINDING INNER PEACE THROUGH MEDITATION

444
00:18:07,853 --> 00:18:10,823
<i>Shall we end the day with a light snack?</i>

445
00:18:10,890 --> 00:18:11,924
<i>- Yes.</i>
<i>- Great.</i>

446
00:18:12,592 --> 00:18:16,228
THEIR RESTING STOP IS NAMED
"MIND-RESTING GAZEBO"

447
00:18:17,129 --> 00:18:18,764
- Wow, they look so good.
- Right.

448
00:18:19,398 --> 00:18:20,533
I'm hungry.

449
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:24,670
ELEGANT ASSORTMENT OF REFRESHMENTS
TO EASE THEIR HUNGER

450
00:18:26,005 --> 00:18:27,640
I didn't get a good look at you until now.

451
00:18:28,207 --> 00:18:30,309
<i>We spent the whole day</i>
<i>bowing side by side.</i>

452
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:32,912
What did you think about
during our meditation?

453
00:18:33,312 --> 00:18:34,814
Nothing.

454
00:18:35,047 --> 00:18:36,115
- Same.
- Really?

455
00:18:36,182 --> 00:18:37,683
<i>Now and then, I took a peek.</i>

456
00:18:37,750 --> 00:18:40,620
<i>I had to focus again</i>
<i>because everyone was deep in meditation.</i>

457
00:18:40,686 --> 00:18:41,954
You said you were hungry.

458
00:18:42,021 --> 00:18:43,389
Bon appétit.

459
00:18:43,723 --> 00:18:45,391
LET ME GET THAT SWEET RICE CAKE

460
00:18:49,795 --> 00:18:50,863
This looks like you.

461
00:18:54,667 --> 00:18:55,601
You know what?

462
00:18:56,102 --> 00:18:57,970
PROTESTING AT THE COMPARISON

463
00:18:58,037 --> 00:18:59,338
- I'm startled.
- Yeah?

464
00:18:59,405 --> 00:19:00,806
Your face isn't that round.

465
00:19:00,873 --> 00:19:02,475
- Right?
- Yeah.

466
00:19:02,541 --> 00:19:03,542
I'M NO LONGER "CIRCLE," OKAY?

467
00:19:03,609 --> 00:19:04,810
Not really, no.

468
00:19:05,011 --> 00:19:06,078
That reminds me.

469
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:08,414
My show is called Hello, Twenty - Wonhee.

470
00:19:08,481 --> 00:19:09,782
So I ask this to all my guests.

471
00:19:09,849 --> 00:19:11,884
What was your life like at 20?

472
00:19:11,951 --> 00:19:12,885
My life at 20?

473
00:19:12,952 --> 00:19:14,420
To be honest,

474
00:19:14,487 --> 00:19:16,055
10 YEARS AGO
I barely remember.

475
00:19:16,122 --> 00:19:17,223
DIDN'T SEE THAT COMING

476
00:19:17,289 --> 00:19:18,190
- Well...
- I get it.

477
00:19:18,257 --> 00:19:21,661
I wasn't really ready to become an adult.

478
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:23,062
It was quite sudden.

479
00:19:23,129 --> 00:19:25,698
Back then, I wasn't particularly excited.

480
00:19:25,765 --> 00:19:28,200
I wasn't ready to turn 20 yet.

481
00:19:28,501 --> 00:19:30,970
I had that sense of panic.

482
00:19:31,037 --> 00:19:31,937
MORE AWKWARD THAN EXCITED

483
00:19:32,338 --> 00:19:33,673
TOTALLY FEELING IT

484
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:35,408
- I get it.
- Was that a response to me

485
00:19:35,474 --> 00:19:36,742
or to the rice cake?

486
00:19:37,343 --> 00:19:40,179
Both, actually.
It was a two-birds-with-one-stone moment.

487
00:19:42,848 --> 00:19:45,685
What was the first thing you tried
when you turned 20?

488
00:19:45,751 --> 00:19:47,153
I just stayed out late.

489
00:19:47,219 --> 00:19:48,821
Minors have to get home early.

490
00:19:48,888 --> 00:19:53,159
But as an adult,
you definitely have more freedom.

491
00:19:53,225 --> 00:19:56,395
You can stay out as late as you want.

492
00:19:56,462 --> 00:19:58,497
You're an adult, after all.

493
00:19:58,564 --> 00:20:00,599
- Because I'm an adult.
- I'm a grown-up.

494
00:20:00,766 --> 00:20:03,202
I hear that you're a total extrovert.

495
00:20:03,269 --> 00:20:05,271
Were you outgoing back in school, too?

496
00:20:05,337 --> 00:20:07,673
- I'm not that outgoing.
- Moderately outgoing?

497
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:10,810
I was a total introvert back in school.

498
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:12,712
- I was the opposite.
- Really?

499
00:20:12,778 --> 00:20:13,946
Back in middle school,

500
00:20:14,013 --> 00:20:15,981
I went crazy and became extroverted.

501
00:20:16,048 --> 00:20:17,717
Ever since I was a little,

502
00:20:17,783 --> 00:20:19,852
- I've always been timid.
- Seriously?

503
00:20:19,919 --> 00:20:21,520
Puberty had made me go crazy.

504
00:20:21,587 --> 00:20:25,825
Social skills are everything
in our line of work.

505
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:29,328
I guess I'm an extrovert by circumstance.

506
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:33,566
I don't think social skills have
anything to do with being an extrovert.

507
00:20:35,568 --> 00:20:38,704
Everyone is so fixated
on the whole MBTI classification.

508
00:20:38,871 --> 00:20:41,040
I want to build
a good relationship with others,

509
00:20:41,107 --> 00:20:43,209
so I pluck up my courage and do my best.

510
00:20:43,275 --> 00:20:46,479
But they would sometimes accuse me
of not being an introvert.

511
00:20:46,545 --> 00:20:47,446
You were doing your best.

512
00:20:47,513 --> 00:20:49,782
That leaves me speechless.

513
00:20:49,849 --> 00:20:51,617
It must be upsetting
to have your efforts ignored.

514
00:20:51,684 --> 00:20:55,154
I used to enjoy talking
about the MBTI classification.

515
00:20:55,221 --> 00:20:56,455
I used it to break the ice, too.

516
00:20:56,522 --> 00:21:00,493
But nowadays,
the whole thing wears me out.

517
00:21:00,559 --> 00:21:02,895
I get it. Not all extroverts are the same.

518
00:21:02,962 --> 00:21:04,463
- Exactly.
- So much generalization.

519
00:21:04,530 --> 00:21:06,832
Are you shy around strangers?

520
00:21:06,899 --> 00:21:09,602
I like people in general,

521
00:21:09,668 --> 00:21:11,504
but I'm still shy around strangers.

522
00:21:11,570 --> 00:21:13,773
I'm the same way,

523
00:21:13,839 --> 00:21:16,208
but I can mask what I'm feeling.

524
00:21:16,776 --> 00:21:18,978
That's cool. How did you learn to do that?

525
00:21:19,211 --> 00:21:22,782
The pressure I get
on variety shows helped.

526
00:21:22,848 --> 00:21:25,718
Wonhee, you're something else.

527
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:26,986
ME?

528
00:21:27,052 --> 00:21:30,055
Basically, you overcame
this obstacle on your own.

529
00:21:30,389 --> 00:21:33,159
- Even though you're an introvert--
- I didn't overcome anything.

530
00:21:33,225 --> 00:21:37,163
- I respond well to training.
- So you think you were born that way?

531
00:21:37,329 --> 00:21:39,431
I guess I'm pretty adaptable.

532
00:21:39,732 --> 00:21:41,634
- I think I am.
- Really?

533
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:45,104
The more I get to know you,
the more mysterious you seem.

534
00:21:45,171 --> 00:21:47,473
You're an enigma.

535
00:21:47,540 --> 00:21:48,607
Thank you.

536
00:21:48,674 --> 00:21:50,075
Did you just thank me?

537
00:21:51,777 --> 00:21:53,546
It's nice, though.

538
00:21:53,612 --> 00:21:56,015
It simply means
you're a multifaceted person.

539
00:21:56,482 --> 00:21:57,316
Thank you.

540
00:21:57,616 --> 00:21:59,051
OUT OF HABIT

541
00:21:59,518 --> 00:22:01,086
Why do you keep thanking me?

542
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:03,622
You look like a quokka when you smile.

543
00:22:03,689 --> 00:22:04,857
So cute.

544
00:22:04,924 --> 00:22:06,158
QUOKKA MIYEON

545
00:22:06,225 --> 00:22:08,527
You said you were shy around strangers.

546
00:22:08,594 --> 00:22:10,696
Do you tend to open up right away,

547
00:22:10,763 --> 00:22:14,033
or does it take time for you to do that?

548
00:22:14,099 --> 00:22:15,901
I usually like people right away.

549
00:22:15,968 --> 00:22:17,236
AMAZED

550
00:22:17,303 --> 00:22:20,406
But it takes me a while to make a friend.

551
00:22:20,472 --> 00:22:21,507
What about you?

552
00:22:21,574 --> 00:22:22,575
I like people in general,

553
00:22:22,641 --> 00:22:24,643
but I have high standards
when it comes to friends.

554
00:22:25,244 --> 00:22:28,480
There are only a few people
who meet the standards.

555
00:22:28,547 --> 00:22:29,515
Tell me, Wonhee.

556
00:22:29,582 --> 00:22:31,450
How many close friends do you have?

557
00:22:31,517 --> 00:22:32,985
- Just 1.
- Just 1?

558
00:22:33,052 --> 00:22:35,287
You must have insanely high standards.

559
00:22:35,354 --> 00:22:37,957
I'm close with my group, obviously.
But apart from them,

560
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:39,225
I only have one close friend.

561
00:22:39,525 --> 00:22:40,559
HOW FASCINATING
Really?

562
00:22:40,626 --> 00:22:43,128
Say you're exhausted from a busy schedule.

563
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:45,865
What do you do to cheer yourself up?

564
00:22:46,265 --> 00:22:47,533
I've come to realize

565
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:51,403
that you need stamina to enjoy anything.

566
00:22:51,470 --> 00:22:54,840
Even something exciting isn't fun
when you're exhausted.

567
00:22:54,907 --> 00:22:57,443
- You can't really focus, right?
- Of course.

568
00:22:57,509 --> 00:23:01,447
I always make an effort to stay healthy.

569
00:23:01,513 --> 00:23:03,315
<i>I never skip meals.</i>

570
00:23:03,582 --> 00:23:04,984
<i>- Meals?</i>
<i>- Yes.</i>

571
00:23:05,618 --> 00:23:08,854
<i>I take supplements on a regular basis.</i>

572
00:23:08,921 --> 00:23:11,557
At the end of the day,
we live pretty irregular lives.

573
00:23:11,790 --> 00:23:12,992
- Yeah.
- So I rest

574
00:23:13,058 --> 00:23:15,461
EVEN ON A BRIEF BREAK
<i>whenever I get the chance.</i>

575
00:23:15,661 --> 00:23:18,597
MIYEON MAKES AN EFFORT TO RECHARGE
<i>I make sure to get plenty of rest.</i>

576
00:23:18,664 --> 00:23:20,199
<i>That is the best we can do.</i>

577
00:23:20,266 --> 00:23:22,968
When do you unwind and recharge?

578
00:23:23,035 --> 00:23:25,070
Being out helps me recharge.

579
00:23:25,137 --> 00:23:27,072
- I'm feeling it now, actually.
- Really?

580
00:23:27,139 --> 00:23:28,774
- Frankly--
- I have to be in my dorm.

581
00:23:28,841 --> 00:23:31,310
When I'm in my room, cleaning,

582
00:23:31,377 --> 00:23:34,980
lying in bed, or sitting at my desk...

583
00:23:35,047 --> 00:23:36,515
- That's when I relax.
- Seriously?

584
00:23:36,582 --> 00:23:37,549
Wait.

585
00:23:37,616 --> 00:23:40,185
Did you ask me that
just so you could say all that?

586
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:41,654
SAW RIGHT THROUGH HER

587
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:42,755
I just don't get it.

588
00:23:42,821 --> 00:23:45,224
How do you relax
when you're out and about?

589
00:23:45,557 --> 00:23:46,926
- I'm doing fine now.
- It's just...

590
00:23:46,992 --> 00:23:48,294
- Really?
- I mean it.

591
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:50,696
- I'm happy to hear it.
- When I'm home,

592
00:23:50,763 --> 00:23:52,464
I keep thinking about tomorrow.

593
00:23:52,531 --> 00:23:54,033
You know that "me time" at home?

594
00:23:54,099 --> 00:23:57,069
I'm not very good at spending time alone.

595
00:23:57,136 --> 00:24:00,072
When I'm out and surrounded by people,

596
00:24:00,139 --> 00:24:02,041
I feel more at ease.

597
00:24:02,107 --> 00:24:04,243
That's what sets introverts
and extroverts apart.

598
00:24:04,310 --> 00:24:05,878
I suppose so.

599
00:24:06,345 --> 00:24:11,317
What goes through your mind
when you need to psych yourself up?

600
00:24:11,383 --> 00:24:13,585
I don't think all that much.

601
00:24:13,652 --> 00:24:17,323
So you don't overthink
or let your imagination run wild?

602
00:24:20,693 --> 00:24:21,894
What's the point of overthinking?

603
00:24:21,961 --> 00:24:23,362
I WANT TO BE LIKE YOU
How admirable.

604
00:24:23,429 --> 00:24:25,597
I think about all sorts of stuff.

605
00:24:25,764 --> 00:24:27,299
Like what to eat later?

606
00:24:27,366 --> 00:24:28,734
Sort of.

607
00:24:28,801 --> 00:24:31,503
Weirdly, I don't crave food
when I'm on a diet.

608
00:24:31,570 --> 00:24:33,505
- Don't lose weight.
- Why not?

609
00:24:33,572 --> 00:24:35,774
- You're cute as you are now.
- Oh, come on.

610
00:24:35,841 --> 00:24:38,177
- You look good now. Don't lose weight.
- Come on.

611
00:24:38,243 --> 00:24:41,947
Isn't it unfair when skinny, hot girlies
tell me not to lose weight?

612
00:24:42,014 --> 00:24:43,449
- I feel--
- Not me.

613
00:24:43,515 --> 00:24:44,750
Look, I'm eating nonstop.

614
00:24:44,817 --> 00:24:45,751
Heard of Changeok Rice Cake?

615
00:24:45,818 --> 00:24:47,119
Yeah, but I've never tried it.

616
00:24:47,186 --> 00:24:48,087
I have some in my van.

617
00:24:48,153 --> 00:24:50,155
I've already had one,
and the rest is also mine.

618
00:24:50,222 --> 00:24:51,690
Nothing for me?

619
00:24:51,757 --> 00:24:53,025
That's so mean.

620
00:24:53,826 --> 00:24:56,128
- Aren't you jealous?
- I'll get some myself later.

621
00:24:56,195 --> 00:24:57,363
It's fabulous.

622
00:24:57,429 --> 00:25:00,566
The sponge cake crumbs
on the rice cake fall off easily,

623
00:25:00,632 --> 00:25:02,034
so you need to be careful.

624
00:25:02,101 --> 00:25:04,203
What's your favorite food?
A snack like this?

625
00:25:04,269 --> 00:25:06,672
Yeah, I enjoy nibbling on light snacks.

626
00:25:06,739 --> 00:25:07,973
<i>I love ramyeon, too.</i>

627
00:25:08,040 --> 00:25:09,108
<i>Ramyeon is amazing.</i>

628
00:25:09,675 --> 00:25:12,811
- I love baked goods and rice cakes.
- Really?

629
00:25:12,878 --> 00:25:15,347
- It must be hard watching what you eat.
- It's a nightmare.

630
00:25:15,414 --> 00:25:19,818
If I have a snack,
I know I'll have to skip a meal.

631
00:25:19,885 --> 00:25:22,454
Snacks never fill me up,
but I still can't stop eating them.

632
00:25:22,521 --> 00:25:23,689
And the cycle repeats.

633
00:25:23,756 --> 00:25:25,190
You sure think a lot.

634
00:25:25,657 --> 00:25:27,493
HABITUAL OVERTHINKER

635
00:25:27,559 --> 00:25:29,128
Do you like working out?

636
00:25:29,194 --> 00:25:30,796
- Not really, right?
- No.

637
00:25:30,863 --> 00:25:34,033
But I've recently started ballet.

638
00:25:34,099 --> 00:25:35,734
- It suits you.
- Here's the thing.

639
00:25:35,801 --> 00:25:38,737
People always laugh when I mention it,
so I usually don't.

640
00:25:38,804 --> 00:25:41,006
- But it's perfect for you.
- I've just picked it up.

641
00:25:41,073 --> 00:25:42,107
Are you flexible?

642
00:25:42,174 --> 00:25:43,609
I am on the flexible side.

643
00:25:43,776 --> 00:25:45,644
- I'm not, so I don't like ballet.
- Really?

644
00:25:45,711 --> 00:25:47,246
My splits are horrible.

645
00:25:47,312 --> 00:25:48,947
I could never have guessed.

646
00:25:49,014 --> 00:25:51,683
- Wonhee, I think...
- Yes?

647
00:25:51,750 --> 00:25:53,952
- You livestream sometimes
- Right.

648
00:25:54,019 --> 00:25:55,687
about cosmetics.

649
00:25:55,754 --> 00:25:58,757
- You're a huge makeup geek.
- I am.

650
00:25:58,824 --> 00:26:00,392
I've bought some items you recommended.

651
00:26:00,626 --> 00:26:02,428
SO HAPPY
Really? That's an honor.

652
00:26:02,494 --> 00:26:05,030
You show which products look better
when mixed together.

653
00:26:05,097 --> 00:26:06,799
VERY PROUD
After watching a few clips,

654
00:26:06,865 --> 00:26:08,667
your videos kept appearing on my feed.

655
00:26:08,734 --> 00:26:11,103
I got hooked and bought a few items
from your videos.

656
00:26:11,170 --> 00:26:12,838
VERY HONORED

657
00:26:12,905 --> 00:26:17,142
You're famous
for being a spectacular beauty.

658
00:26:17,209 --> 00:26:18,410
No, I'm not.

659
00:26:18,477 --> 00:26:20,512
I'm over that phase now.

660
00:26:21,046 --> 00:26:23,215
- How come?
- It was all for a bit.

661
00:26:23,282 --> 00:26:28,387
Are there moments when you think,
"Jeez, I look stunning"?

662
00:26:28,454 --> 00:26:30,089
After I get my hair and makeup done.

663
00:26:30,155 --> 00:26:33,192
<i>The moment I look in the mirror,</i>
<i>I feel like a whole new person.</i>

664
00:26:33,258 --> 00:26:34,460
I know what you mean.

665
00:26:34,526 --> 00:26:36,195
- I also get shocked.
- You do?

666
00:26:36,261 --> 00:26:37,763
"How did this happen?"

667
00:26:37,830 --> 00:26:39,998
- I'm sure you look the same.
- Oh, no.

668
00:26:40,065 --> 00:26:43,068
The makeup artists practically sculpt me
a new nose every time.

669
00:26:43,135 --> 00:26:45,270
I'm like, "Huh?"

670
00:26:45,337 --> 00:26:48,207
Sometimes, I even feel guilty
because I look so different.

671
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:49,408
What? No way.

672
00:26:49,475 --> 00:26:50,709
I really feel guilty.

673
00:26:50,776 --> 00:26:54,379
You must know full well
that you're super cute.

674
00:26:54,446 --> 00:26:58,317
I have that youthful look,
and I'm not fully satisfied with it.

675
00:26:58,383 --> 00:27:00,853
I'm not cutesy and sweet,
personality-wise.

676
00:27:00,919 --> 00:27:02,855
So it feels like false advertising.

677
00:27:02,921 --> 00:27:05,891
- I mean, I'm not all that cute.
- Look.

678
00:27:06,525 --> 00:27:08,327
But everyone tells me I am.

679
00:27:08,393 --> 00:27:09,661
And that's a compliment.

680
00:27:09,728 --> 00:27:11,964
Deep down,
I know that and enjoy hearing it.

681
00:27:12,030 --> 00:27:13,899
That really gives me the ick.

682
00:27:13,966 --> 00:27:15,901
That's exactly what I go through.

683
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:17,035
- Me too.
- You feel me, right?

684
00:27:17,102 --> 00:27:19,605
When I review my work
and catch myself acting cute,

685
00:27:19,671 --> 00:27:21,173
- I feel like puking.
- I get it.

686
00:27:21,240 --> 00:27:24,276
Now that I think about it,
you're not the soft type.

687
00:27:24,343 --> 00:27:27,079
You look like a cute little angel,

688
00:27:27,146 --> 00:27:28,447
but you're actually laid-back.

689
00:27:28,514 --> 00:27:29,815
Even calling myself laid-back

690
00:27:29,882 --> 00:27:31,083
- gives me the ick.
- Yeah?

691
00:27:31,550 --> 00:27:33,685
- It's just funny. Don't you agree?
- I get it.

692
00:27:33,752 --> 00:27:37,623
- You were just born with a cute face
- I'm not all that chill.

693
00:27:37,689 --> 00:27:39,258
- and a chill soul.
- I'm not chill.

694
00:27:39,324 --> 00:27:40,526
I can hold a grudge.

695
00:27:40,592 --> 00:27:43,061
When someone asks,
"You know you're cute, right?"

696
00:27:43,128 --> 00:27:43,962
I'm lost.

697
00:27:44,029 --> 00:27:46,965
Even if I deny that,
they're like, "Yeah, right."

698
00:27:47,032 --> 00:27:48,367
It's a nightmare.

699
00:27:48,433 --> 00:27:51,870
See? That's how I got caught up
in the princess mess.

700
00:27:51,937 --> 00:27:55,374
But I can't even say,
"Yes, I'm very cute."

701
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:57,442
- You feel me, right?
- Of course.

702
00:27:57,509 --> 00:27:58,744
A queen like you should get it.

703
00:27:58,977 --> 00:28:01,647
- I get where you're coming from.
- Right?

704
00:28:01,713 --> 00:28:04,783
PRINCESS MIYEON'S DEFENSE
I never thought I was that pretty.

705
00:28:04,850 --> 00:28:07,486
But my team always does their best
to glam me up.

706
00:28:07,553 --> 00:28:09,788
Objectively speaking, I'm not bad-looking.

707
00:28:09,855 --> 00:28:11,356
- You're stunning.
- So basically--

708
00:28:11,423 --> 00:28:12,724
You're downright beautiful.

709
00:28:12,791 --> 00:28:13,659
Accept it, okay?

710
00:28:13,725 --> 00:28:15,594
You're cute. Accept that, too.

711
00:28:15,661 --> 00:28:19,097
Anyway, it doesn't feel right
to reject their compliments.

712
00:28:19,164 --> 00:28:22,034
When you deny a compliment,
things get awkward, right?

713
00:28:22,100 --> 00:28:23,735
While thanking people
for their kind words,

714
00:28:23,802 --> 00:28:26,438
I somehow ended up creating
this princess persona.

715
00:28:26,505 --> 00:28:29,541
At first, I just thanked them.
Then I started adding, "Yeah, I'm pretty."

716
00:28:29,741 --> 00:28:32,544
And gradually,
I got too committed to the bit.

717
00:28:32,611 --> 00:28:33,579
I see.

718
00:28:33,645 --> 00:28:35,113
The whole bit took hold of me.

719
00:28:35,180 --> 00:28:36,882
I kept rolling with it for a while.

720
00:28:36,949 --> 00:28:39,318
But that's not who I really am.

721
00:28:39,384 --> 00:28:41,687
- Right?
- Did it ever become a burden?

722
00:28:41,753 --> 00:28:43,922
Well, I wasn't affected that much.

723
00:28:43,989 --> 00:28:45,490
- You really got into character.
- I guess so.

724
00:28:45,557 --> 00:28:46,959
It didn't really bother me.

725
00:28:47,025 --> 00:28:48,827
I made all those silly comments as a joke.

726
00:28:48,894 --> 00:28:51,063
But even my mom asked me this.

727
00:28:51,129 --> 00:28:54,366
"You don't honestly believe
what you're saying, right?"

728
00:28:54,433 --> 00:28:57,069
People around me
actually started worrying.

729
00:28:57,135 --> 00:28:58,637
I realized it was time...

730
00:28:58,704 --> 00:29:00,172
- To dial things down?
- Yes.

731
00:29:00,239 --> 00:29:02,207
I decided it was time
to leave that phase behind.

732
00:29:02,274 --> 00:29:06,144
So can you switch personas on and off?

733
00:29:06,211 --> 00:29:08,981
You make it look so easy.

734
00:29:09,047 --> 00:29:10,983
"Yep, I'm pretty. Bye!"

735
00:29:11,049 --> 00:29:12,384
- You then turn it off.
- I can do that.

736
00:29:12,451 --> 00:29:14,253
When you need it, you turn it back on.

737
00:29:14,319 --> 00:29:17,189
I can do that at will because I like both.

738
00:29:17,823 --> 00:29:19,591
HAS HIGH SELF-ESTEEM
Both are great.

739
00:29:19,758 --> 00:29:22,728
Lately, I've been questioning that.

740
00:29:22,794 --> 00:29:25,731
You and your group, i-dle,

741
00:29:25,797 --> 00:29:28,200
<i>have been working together</i>
<i>for a long time.</i>

742
00:29:28,267 --> 00:29:29,735
<i>You've renewed your contracts</i>
<i>several times.</i>

743
00:29:29,801 --> 00:29:33,705
What's the secret
to staying together for so long?

744
00:29:34,339 --> 00:29:36,441
Honestly, arguing helps.

745
00:29:36,508 --> 00:29:38,377
That's how we are.

746
00:29:38,443 --> 00:29:39,711
We never argue.

747
00:29:39,911 --> 00:29:43,181
You never argue?
Do you always understand each other?

748
00:29:43,248 --> 00:29:44,750
It works for my group

749
00:29:44,816 --> 00:29:48,453
<i>because everyone is</i>
<i>easygoing and kindhearted.</i>

750
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:52,291
So not a single one of you
is confrontational?

751
00:29:52,357 --> 00:29:53,392
Not really, no.

752
00:29:53,458 --> 00:29:55,694
No matter how close you get
with your members,

753
00:29:55,761 --> 00:29:57,296
you can never fully understand them.

754
00:29:57,562 --> 00:30:02,634
I believe everyone thinks
and expresses themselves differently.

755
00:30:02,701 --> 00:30:07,172
Even if you think
you're being considerate,

756
00:30:07,239 --> 00:30:10,275
it can still lead to frustration

757
00:30:10,342 --> 00:30:13,312
if you don't communicate clearly.

758
00:30:13,378 --> 00:30:15,213
Idols have to spend a long time

759
00:30:15,280 --> 00:30:16,982
- with their members.
- Right.

760
00:30:17,049 --> 00:30:20,752
For us, talking things through
whenever we had a conflict really helped.

761
00:30:20,819 --> 00:30:25,424
When I ask veteran idols
for their secret to good teamwork,

762
00:30:25,490 --> 00:30:28,026
everyone tells me, "Fight a lot."

763
00:30:28,093 --> 00:30:30,829
Of course, it doesn't have to be physical.

764
00:30:31,063 --> 00:30:32,664
NOTED

765
00:30:32,731 --> 00:30:35,100
This is the final segment of my show.

766
00:30:35,167 --> 00:30:37,069
- Already?
- We've reached that point.

767
00:30:37,135 --> 00:30:40,706
I always ask this question
to all my guests.

768
00:30:41,006 --> 00:30:43,408
Could you give me advice on turning 20?

769
00:30:43,475 --> 00:30:44,643
- Advice?
- Yes.

770
00:30:44,710 --> 00:30:46,078
I'd appreciate it.

771
00:30:46,912 --> 00:30:51,583
First of all,
congratulations on turning 20.

772
00:30:51,650 --> 00:30:54,720
I mean, it's a beautiful age.

773
00:30:54,786 --> 00:30:58,724
You must've worked long and hard
preparing for your debut.

774
00:30:58,790 --> 00:31:01,727
Now that you have turned 20,

775
00:31:01,793 --> 00:31:05,497
I hope you make
plenty of time for yourself

776
00:31:05,564 --> 00:31:08,867
and try everything
you've always wanted to do

777
00:31:09,668 --> 00:31:11,470
in that golden year.

778
00:31:11,536 --> 00:31:13,472
- Thank you.
- I should thank you.

779
00:31:13,538 --> 00:31:15,974
I really appreciate it.

780
00:31:17,542 --> 00:31:19,978
- Do you feel rested now?
- Yes.

781
00:31:20,045 --> 00:31:21,079
Great.

782
00:31:21,146 --> 00:31:25,217
At first, I simply thought
I had two pretty participants.

783
00:31:25,283 --> 00:31:26,818
Over the course of the program,

784
00:31:26,885 --> 00:31:29,454
I discovered that you're beautiful
inside and out.

785
00:31:29,521 --> 00:31:31,857
It made me want to root for both of you.

786
00:31:31,923 --> 00:31:34,059
Here are the wish candles.

787
00:31:34,459 --> 00:31:37,195
<i>Write down your name and wish.</i>

788
00:31:37,763 --> 00:31:39,464
<i>- Thank you.</i>
<i>- My name?</i>

789
00:31:39,531 --> 00:31:40,565
My name is...

790
00:31:44,503 --> 00:31:48,073
MY FAMILY'S HAPPINESS AND WELL-BEING

791
00:31:49,508 --> 00:31:52,577
...FOR MANY YEARS TO COME

792
00:31:52,911 --> 00:31:55,013
WISH CANDLES READY

793
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:56,615
What did you put?

794
00:31:56,681 --> 00:31:59,151
I put, "My family's happiness
and well-being."

795
00:31:59,785 --> 00:32:00,952
That's what I wrote.

796
00:32:01,019 --> 00:32:02,687
Was I being too selfish?

797
00:32:02,754 --> 00:32:04,055
- Don't worry about it.
- I wrote,

798
00:32:04,122 --> 00:32:05,924
"May I stay healthy and cheerful

799
00:32:05,991 --> 00:32:08,560
so I can continue to work
for many years to come."

800
00:32:08,627 --> 00:32:10,395
Work never even crossed my mind.

801
00:32:10,462 --> 00:32:12,230
OFF THEY GO WITH THEIR WISH CANDLES

802
00:32:12,531 --> 00:32:13,632
<i>Oh, I'm full.</i>

803
00:32:14,733 --> 00:32:17,769
- No trouble writing your wishes?
- None.

804
00:32:17,836 --> 00:32:21,339
Light your candle
and place it inside the case.

805
00:32:21,406 --> 00:32:22,240
WITH HER WHOLE HEART

806
00:32:22,307 --> 00:32:23,608
WONHEE'S CANDLE IS ALL SET

807
00:32:27,412 --> 00:32:29,881
MIYEON'S CANDLE IS ALSO ALL SET

808
00:32:30,348 --> 00:32:31,416
There.

809
00:32:32,584 --> 00:32:35,454
THEY TAKE A HALF BOW,
HOPING THEIR WISHES WILL COME TRUE

810
00:32:39,157 --> 00:32:42,060
"BE KIND TO YOURSELF
AND MAKE THE MOST OF THE PRECIOUS TIME"

811
00:32:42,127 --> 00:32:43,361
So many cute items.

812
00:32:43,662 --> 00:32:44,930
That's so cute.

813
00:32:45,130 --> 00:32:47,532
RIGHT UP WONHEE'S ALLEY
This is so pretty. I dig it.

814
00:32:47,599 --> 00:32:48,733
GOAL: FIGURE OUT WONHEE'S TASTE

815
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:50,168
EPISODE 7 GIRLIE
CHARLES

816
00:32:50,602 --> 00:32:53,238
IN SEARCH OF TASTE WITH THE GIRLIE'S HELP

817
00:32:53,305 --> 00:32:55,073
- I've already picked one out.
- Show me.

818
00:32:55,140 --> 00:32:56,241
This one.

819
00:32:57,776 --> 00:32:58,977
HER TASTE WILL SHOCK YOU
Isn't it cute?

820
00:32:59,511 --> 00:33:01,112
How's this? It caught my eye right away.

821
00:33:01,179 --> 00:33:02,280
WONHEE'S TASTE IS JUST AS SHOCKING

822
00:33:02,347 --> 00:33:04,182
What about this? It's pretty cute.

823
00:33:05,250 --> 00:33:08,053
THIS GIRLIE HAS HER STANDARDS

824
00:33:08,320 --> 00:33:10,355
THE GAP BETWEEN THEM WIDENS

825
00:33:10,689 --> 00:33:13,391
I thought I was so savvy and cunning.

826
00:33:13,458 --> 00:33:15,060
I don't think that way.

827
00:33:15,126 --> 00:33:16,761
Whoever texts me is a flirt.

828
00:33:17,362 --> 00:33:18,964
FACED WITH ENDLESS DIFFERENCES

829
00:33:19,030 --> 00:33:20,398
WILL WONHEE FIND HER TASTE?

830
00:33:20,465 --> 00:33:22,234
Subtitle translation by Jeongwoo Kim
